        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(cli): suppress mcp serve startup stdout",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where stdio MCP clients launching `openclaw mcp serve` could receive doctor or config-warning text on stdout before JSON-RPC messages, causing protocol parse failures.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`mcp serve` now uses the existing stdout-clean CLI startup policy. This routes startup diagnostics away from protocol stdout before config preflight runs, while leaving other non-JSON commands unchanged.\n\nThe focused regression covers the complete startup-policy result for `[\"mcp\", \"serve\"]`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nMCP clients can launch OpenClaw's stdio server without non-JSON startup output corrupting the protocol stream.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Original live reproduction:\n  - before: `openclaw mcp serve` emitted 740 stdout bytes of config-warning output\n  - after: startup emitted 0 stdout bytes\n  - affected clients stopped accumulating fresh `Failed to parse JSONRPC message` errors after restart\n- Rebased onto current `main` with the original two-file behavior preserved.\n- Static validation:\n  - `git diff --check`\n  - `node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check src/cli/command-startup-policy.ts src/cli/command-startup-policy.test.ts`\n- Fresh structured autoreview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Fresh exact-head hosted Ubuntu CI is running on `bfa3bf4caa80a44f64918eaabbb6198a590acb11`.\n\nAI-assisted maintainer rebase/review; the contributor's PR and credit are preserved.\n",
